<h2>2. 12-Step Step-by-Step Practical Demonstration Protocol</h2>

<h3>Step 1: Student Command Dashboard (/dashboard)</h3>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> Open <code>http://localhost:3000/dashboard</code>.<br>
<strong>Point Out:</strong> Header greeting with real-time Asia/Kolkata date: <strong>Sat, 31 Oct 2026</strong>. 4 metric tiles (Upcoming Deadlines, Active Courses, Tasks Pending, Overall Progress). Today's prioritized tasks with factor badges. 7-day cognitive workload distribution chart.</p>
<div class="say-box">
  "AcademicAI grounds every view in the current academic date—October 31, 2026. Deadlines are prioritized deterministically based on deadline proximity and course weightage to prevent cognitive overload."
</div>

<h3>Step 2: Ingesting an Unstructured Academic Notice (/inbox)</h3>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> Open <code>/inbox</code>. Paste the circular:<br>
<em>"All students registered in Natural Language Processing (CSE4001) must submit their Capstone Project Interim Report on Canvas by this Wednesday, November 4, 2026 at 11:59 PM IST. Weightage: 20 marks. Late submissions will incur a 2-mark penalty."</em><br>
Click <strong>Analyze Notice</strong>.<br>
<strong>Verify:</strong> Extracted Category: ASSIGNMENT/PROJECT, Course: CSE4001, Platform: Canvas, Normalized Deadline: Nov 4, 2026 11:59 PM IST, Priority: HIGH (Score: 65). Click <strong>Confirm & Create Task</strong>.</p>
<div class="say-box">
  "The NLP pipeline extracts the academic intent, course code, submission platform, and normalizes the conversational relative deadline into an absolute timestamp in Indian Standard Time."
</div>

<h3>Step 3: Demonstrating 5-Way Notice Change Intelligence</h3>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> In <code>/inbox</code>, paste the rescheduled circular:<br>
<em>"Due to the upcoming placement drive, the Capstone Project Interim Report deadline originally due on November 4 has been postponed to Saturday, November 7, 2026 at 5:00 PM IST on Canvas."</em><br>
Click <strong>Analyze Notice</strong>.<br>
<strong>Verify:</strong> Notice Relationship Badge: <code>RESCHEDULED</code>. Audit Diff: Nov 4 &rarr; Nov 7. Click <strong>Apply Reschedule</strong>.</p>
<div class="say-box">
  "AcademicAI does not create a redundant task. Its 5-way change intelligence recognizes this as a reschedule, logs an immutable diff, and updates the existing deliverable."
</div>

<h3>Step 4: Circular Cancellation & Zero Fabrication Check</h3>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> In <code>/inbox</code>, paste:<br>
<em>"Tomorrow's guest lecture in SJT 402 has been cancelled due to speaker illness."</em><br>
<strong>Verify:</strong> Category: CLASS_CANCELLATION, Relationship: CANCELLED. Status marked CANCELLED and purged from the active cognitive workload radar.</p>

<h3>Step 5: Task Management & Verifiable Evidence Drawer (/tasks)</h3>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> Navigate to <code>/tasks</code>. Click on any task row.<br>
<strong>Verify:</strong> Opens the Evidence Drawer displaying the exact verbatim snippet from the source notice. Demonstrates zero hallucination.</p>

<h3>Step 6: Dynamic Syllabus Calendar (/calendar)</h3>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> Navigate to <code>/calendar</code>.<br>
<strong>Verify:</strong> Month view renders October 2026 with today (Oct 31) highlighted with a purple TODAY badge. Click <strong>Next Month (&gt;)</strong> to see November 2026 with the rescheduled task. Click <strong>Prev Month (&lt;)</strong> to see preserved historical September records.</p>

<h3>Step 7: Cognitive Workload Radar & Risk Assessment (/analytics)</h3>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> Navigate to <code>/analytics</code>.<br>
<strong>Verify:</strong> Workload radar highlights 48-hour assessment clusters and explains quiet-hours notification suppression.</p>

<h3>Step 8: Academic Assistant with Grounded Gating (/assistant)</h3>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> Ask: <em>"What are my deadlines for CSE4001 this week?"</em> (Grounds strictly on database tasks).<br>
Ask: <em>"Delete all my tasks for tomorrow."</em> (Enforces mandatory destructive mutation confirmation gating).</p>

<h3>Step 9: Switching to Faculty Portal (Dr. P. Raman)</h3>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> Open <code>/faculty-course-intelligence</code>.<br>
<strong>Verify:</strong> Header displays <strong>Dr. P. Raman (FAC-NLP-01)</strong>. Scoped strictly to <strong>CSE4001</strong>. Cohort of 60 students (42 Submitted, 18 Not Submitted, 7 Overdue). Assessment collision warnings displayed.</p>

<h3>Step 10: Syllabus & Rubric Management (/rubrics, /syllabus)</h3>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> Open <code>/rubrics</code>.<br>
<strong>Verify:</strong> 5-criterion Capstone rubric with criterion weights summing to exactly 100%.</p>

<h3>Step 11: AI-Assisted Submission Evaluation (/faculty-review)</h3>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> Open <code>/faculty-review</code>. Select student <code>21BDS0142</code> and click <strong>Evaluate Submission</strong>.<br>
<strong>Verify:</strong> Suggests score <strong>82.5 / 100</strong> across 5 criteria, with verbatim explanatory quotes extracted from student document. Operates with 100% reliability via offline deterministic fallback if internet is unavailable.</p>

<h3>Step 12: Faculty Approval & Permanent Grade Commitment</h3>
<p><strong>Action:</strong> Adjust documentation slider from 16 to 18. Enter professor feedback. Click <strong>Approve & Finalize Grade</strong>.<br>
<strong>Verify:</strong> Badge changes to green <strong>GRADED (84.5 / 100)</strong>, committing permanently to SQLite.</p>

